.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KFIRE-EXPORTER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kfire-exporter
.Nd count Firecracker microVMs where node_exporter will serve them
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The estate dashboards count virtual machines from libvirt, and a
Firecracker microVM made by
.Xr kfire 8
is not a libvirt domain.
.Nm
counts them from kfire's records, so that the dashboards can add them in.
It writes:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ql kldload_firecracker_instances
Every microVM kfire has a record for.
.It Ql kldload_firecracker_running
Those whose
.Pa kfire- Ns Ar name Ns Pa .service
is active.
.It Ql kldload_firecracker_by_golden{golden}
How many were made from each golden.
.It Ql kldload_firecracker_instance{name,golden,ip,vcpus,ram_mb}
One per microVM: 1 while it runs, else 0.
.El
.Pp
The file is written under a temporary name and renamed over the real one.
When node_exporter's textfile directory does not exist it writes nothing.
.Pa kfire-exporter.timer
runs it 10 seconds after boot and every 15 seconds after that, as root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0, writing nothing.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/kfire/instances/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /instance.json
What it reads; the golden, address, processors and memory come from
here, through
.Xr jq 1
when it is installed.
.It Pa /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile_collector/kfire.prom
What it writes.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0, always: an empty or missing file already means
.Dq no data
to Prometheus, and a failing timer would only be noise.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop with no microVMs on 2026-09-30:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cat /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile_collector/kfire.prom
# HELP kldload_firecracker_instances Firecracker microVMs kfire has a record for.
# TYPE kldload_firecracker_instances gauge
kldload_firecracker_instances 0
# HELP kldload_firecracker_running Firecracker microVMs whose unit is active.
# TYPE kldload_firecracker_running gauge
kldload_firecracker_running 0
# HELP kldload_firecracker_by_golden Firecracker microVMs per golden template.
# TYPE kldload_firecracker_by_golden gauge
# HELP kldload_firecracker_instance One line per microVM; 1 when its unit is active.
# TYPE kldload_firecracker_instance gauge
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
Whether node_exporter read the directory cleanly:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:9100/metrics | grep -E '^(kldload_firecracker_running|node_textfile_scrape_error)'
kldload_firecracker_running 0
node_textfile_scrape_error 0
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr arcstats-exporter 8 ,
.Xr kfire 8 ,
.Xr zpool-scrub-exporter 8
.Sh HISTORY
Written after 2026-09-06, when microVMs were cloned on a lab host during
a demonstration of the fleet and the dashboard's machine count read 39
before and 39 after.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Without
.Xr jq 1
every microVM is still counted, but with no address, processors or
memory.
